{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":557,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","line":913,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Smoothness of the Horizontal Projection of a Vector Field]\n\\label{lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth}\n\n\\uses{lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth, lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth, def:horizontal-space}\n\n\n\n\nFor smooth $W$ on $\\tilde M$, the field $W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi_x(W_x))$ is smooth.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Lemma \\ref{lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth} makes $x\\mapsto d\\pi_x(W_x)$ a smooth section along $\\pi$, and Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth} lifts it smoothly.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Smoothness of the Horizontal Projection of a Vector Field] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d70726f6a656374696f6e2d6669656c642d736d6f6f7468\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apushforward-along-map-smooth\">↗ lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-along-smooth\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-space\">↗ def:horizontal-space</a> <p></p>For smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde M$\">$\\tilde M$</span>, the field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi _x(W_x))$\">$W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi _x(W_x))$</span> is smooth.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apushforward-along-map-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a70757368666f72776172642d616c6f6e672d6d61702d736d6f6f7468\">7</a> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\mapsto d\\pi _x(W_x)$\">$x\\mapsto d\\pi _x(W_x)$</span> a smooth section along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi $\">$\\pi $</span>, and Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-along-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d616c6f6e672d736d6f6f7468\">7</a> lifts it smoothly. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth","title":"lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth","label":"lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth","label":"lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space","title":"def:horizontal-space","label":"def:horizontal-space"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties","title":"prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties","label":"prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Smoothness of the Horizontal Projection of a Vector Field]\n\\label{lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth}\n\n\\uses{lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth, lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth, def:horizontal-space}\n\n\n\n\nFor smooth $W$ on $\\tilde M$, the field $W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi_x(W_x))$ is smooth.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Lemma \\ref{lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth} makes $x\\mapsto d\\pi_x(W_x)$ a smooth section along $\\pi$, and Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth} lifts it smoothly.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth","title":"lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-along-smooth","description":""},{"node"